'''Prestige Group''' is an Indian [[real estate development]] company headquartered in [[Bangalore]].<ref>[https://www.businesstoday.in/latest/corporate/story/how-irfan-razack-and-his-brothers-parlayed-a-small-time-haberdashery-in-bangalore-to-become-one-of-indias-largest-real-estate-companies-65301-2016-12-26 Bangalore's 'local boys': From haberdashery to real-estate giant] – ''Business Today''. 26 December 2016. Retrieved 13 October 2025.</ref> Founded by Razack Sattar in 1986, Prestige has developed residential colonies and commercial spaces in [[Bangalore]], [[Chennai]], [[Kochi]], [[Kozhikode|Calicut]], [[Hyderabad]], [[Mumbai]], [[Mangalore]], Goa and [[National Capital Region (India)|Delhi-NCR]].<ref>{{Cite news |date=5 February 2025 |title=Prestige Group expanding its mall portfolio with new properties in Mumbai and Delhi-NCR |url=https://www.hindustantimes.com/real-estate/prestige-group-expanding-its-mall-portfolio-with-new-properties-in-mumbai-and-delhincr-101738741426476.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250209022352/https://www.hindustantimes.com/real-estate/prestige-group-expanding-its-mall-portfolio-with-new-properties-in-mumbai-and-delhincr-101738741426476.html |archive-date=9 February 2025 |access-date=17 July 2025 |work=Hindustan Times |language=en-us}}</ref>

Notable projects include [[Prestige Shantiniketan]], [[UB City]], [[Prestige Golfshire]], Prestige Acropolis, [[Nexus Mall (Koramangala)|The Forum]], The Forum Value, [[Nexus Vijaya Mall|The Forum Vijaya]], [[Nexus Celebration Mall|The Celebration Mall]], Prestige Lakeside Habitat, The Prestige City and [[Prestige Kingfisher Towers]].

==History==
Prestige Group was founded by Razack Sattar, a [[Kutchi Memon]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=26 December 2016 |title=Bangalore's 'local boys': From middlemen to biggest real estate agent |url=https://www.businesstoday.in/latest/corporate/story/how-irfan-razack-and-his-brothers-parlayed-a-small-time-haberdashery-in-bangalore-to-become-one-of-indias-largest-real-estate-companies-65301-2016-12-26 |access-date=21 June 2022 |website=Business Today |language=en}}</ref> During the 1960s and late 1970s his sons [[Irfan Razack]] and [[Rezwan Razack]] worked with him, and his youngest son Noaman Razack also joined when the business grew.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.prestigeconstructions.com/pdf/annual-report-2010-11.pdf|title=Annual Report 2010-2011 - Prestige Group|publisher=Prestige Group|access-date=10 April 2014}}</ref> It began as a retail business, but moved to real estate with its first project, Prestige Court, at KH Road in Bangalore in 1985.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.cyberoam.com/downloads/CaseStudies/PrestigeEstatesProjectsLtdCaseStudy.pdf|title=Prestige Estates Projects Ltd - Case Study|publisher=Cyberoam|access-date=10 April 2014}}</ref>

